  "report_period": "Week 33 (13th Aug to 20th Aug 2021)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Panamax \"Priscilla Venture\" 77/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 03/2023) was committed to Chinese buyers for USD 18,25 mill, while a week ago the \"Lemessos Queen\" 76/2008 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2023, DD 10/2021, BWTS fitted) was sold at mid-high USD 18 mill. Asia Pacific Shipping sold three Ultramax sister vessels, the \"Asia Ruby III\" 63/2014 Jinling, China (SS/DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) for low-mid USD 22 mill including T/C attached, the \"Asia Ruby II\" 63/2014 Jinling, China (SS 04/2024, DD 04/2022, BWTS fitted) for low-mid USD 24 mill basis prompt delivery and the \"Asia Ruby IV\" 63/2014 Jinling, China (SS 07/2024, DD 08/2022, BWTS fitted) for high USD 23 mill. In addition, the \"Nord Peak\" 61/2011 Oshima, Japan (SS 03/2026, DD 05/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold to Hong Kong buyers for USD 22,5 mill. The Supramax \"Atlantic Ensenada\" 55/2006 Kawasaki, Japan (SS/DD 04/2023) of Pacific Carriers was committed to Bangladeshi buyers for USD 15,7 mill. Note that a week ago, the two-years-younger \"Aditya\" 55/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 02/2023) was sold for USD 16,5 mill basis delivery September-October 2021. On the Handysize sector, the \"Nereus Island\" 38/2014 Imabari, Japan (SS 04/2024, DD 03/2022) from Yahata Kisen was sold to Pacific Basin for USD 21 mill, whilst Masumoto Shipping sold the one-year-younger \"Pacific Bulker\" 36/2015 Shikoku, Japan (SS 10/2024, DD 10/2022) for USD 21 mill also. Moreover, Premuda sold their \"Four Diamond\" 34/2011 Pha Rung, Vietnam (SS/DD 10/2021) to UAE buyers for mid-high USD 12 mill & the two- years-younger sister vessel \"Four Emerald\" 34/2013 Pha Rung, Vietnam (SS/DD 04/2023, BWTS fitted) to Turkish buyers Deval Shipping for low USD 15 mill.",
    "tankers": "Thenamaris have sold their Aframax \"Seafalcon\" 112/2002 Samho, Korea (SS/DD 02/2022) to Chinese buyers for USD 13,5 mill. Note that three weeks ago, the one-year-younger \"Astro Saturn\" 105/2003 Daewoo, Korea (SS 04/2023, DD 08/2021) was sold at USD 12,4 mill. The LR1 \"Cabo Kamui\" 74/2016 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 11/2021, BWTS fitted) & the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Cabo Misaki\" 74/2017 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 03/2022, BWTS fitted) of Nisshin Shipping were sold to Chilean buyers Ultratank for USD 31,5 mill each. Remind you that back in June, the sister vessel \"Nord Lavender\" 74/2017 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 07/2022, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 31 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low usd 15,00's fio range. South East Asian trips via South Africa into China were fixed around usd 40,000/42,000 pd. / no period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 29,000/30,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into Japan were reported fixed in the usd 31,000/32,000 pd. South East Asian trips via ECSA into China were reported at the level of usd 34,000/35,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were fixed around usd 33,500/34,500 pd. West African trips via North Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 31,000/32,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via Baltic were reported at the level of usd 36,000/38,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via North Coast South America or US East Coast were fixed around usd 30,000/31,000 pd. Continental trips via Baltic into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 35,000/36,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 48,000/49,000 pd. On the period front a Kamsarmax were reported fixed in the usd 30,000 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery in the Pacific.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into India were reported fixed at the level of usd 34,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 130K. South East Asian trips via Indonesia into China were reported at the level of usd 37,000/38,000 pd. Indian trips via South Africa into India were fixed around usd 34,000/35,000 pd. Continental trips into East Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 40,000 pd. South American trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 41,500/42,500 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Indonesian trips into Japan with metcoke were reported at the level of usd 38,000/39,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 35,000/36,000 pd. West African trips via Black Sea into US West Coast were reported at the level of usd 30,000/31,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into US Gulf with cement were fixed around usd 42,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 30,000 pd. US Gulf trips into ECSA were fixed around usd 32,000/33,000 pd. A small Handysize was fixed on period at the usd 18,000 pd basis delivery NCSA for 2 years employment."
    }
  },
